Yeah, but it's still a waste to prep against them.
Helm (brilliance/telepathy/etc) + small shield + boots
(speed/jumping/etc) + gloves + DSM + t-shirt + cloak all enchanted to
+4:
AC -32
The same, but all of it whataver combination of thoroughly rusty
thoroughly burnt thoroughly corroded  etc that it can get:
AC -27

The worst that rust, fire, corrosion, etc can do to any of the normal
"keeper" armor is 1 AC except for a robe (where it can do 2).

If you have unused ?enchant armor and any armor that hasn't been fully
enchanted yet, you're much better off using it to enchant the armor
than to fooproof it.

I ascend all the time with rusty/burnt/etc armor.  Even if I have the
spare ?enchant armor by the end, it's not worth the effort to fix
it--you'll have plenty low AC (to the point where those extra few
points don't make a difference) without bothering.

The water-walking boots I mention are the exception only so you can
walk on lava.

If you find random cursed ?destroy armor around the dungeon then you
may as well use them to fooproof stuff.

Weapons are a somewhat different matter but the normal ways to get a
decent one (sacrificing at an altar or #dipping for excalibur) make it
rustproof automatically.  If you wind up with a decent weapon that
isn't rustproof, though, it _is_ worth using a ?enchant weapon on that
(in large part because you're normally swimming in ?enchant weapon
anyway).



